  "body": "What happens: The release gate of the v0.20.0 cut failed in step 02 (kernel suites) after 3 minutes. No gate before the cut runs the kernel suites: the batch tier (the post-merge gate) omits them, and the quick tier runs them only when `crates/kernel` changes. The failure showed only at the cut. `cargo xtask gate` also has no option to run only the failed step again, so a fix for one step costs a full run of about 90 minutes.\n\nWanted:\n- The batch tier runs the debug suites of `camcraft-kernel` (`cargo test -p camcraft-kernel`, about 3 minutes). The post-merge gate then finds a kernel failure on main before a cut.\n- `cargo xtask gate <tier>` gets an option that runs only the named steps (for example `--only kernel`, repeatable), and an option that runs only the steps that failed in a given `gate-logs/<run>` directory.\n- `--dry-run` shows the selected steps.\n- `xtask/src/plan.rs` unit tests pin both changes.\n- AGENTS.md (\"Three gate tiers\") states the change.\n\nEvidence: `gate-logs/release-20261114-185541/02-kernel_suites.log` (`step_files_agree_or_refuse_by_name`, issue 1697). Maintainer, 2026-11-14: \"catch kernel lanes in the xtask gate.. so we dont have to start over 3 times\".\n\nDone means: `cargo xtask gate batch --dry-run` lists the kernel suites, the two options work and have unit tests, and the PR body carries `Process change: yes`.\n",
